Let no-unknown-parameters accept the rejection reason of a promise callback.

At 13909c9, the rule reports each `unknown` parameter that is not named `cause` and is not the
subject of a type predicate. The rejection reason of `.catch()` and `.then()` is `any`, so
`typescript/use-unknown-in-catch-callback-variable` asks for `(error: unknown) => ...`, and
`unicorn/catch-error-name` asks for the name `error`. The rule then reports every way to write the
callback. The callback cannot parse the reason before it receives it.

The patch skips the first parameter of a function that is the first argument of `.catch()` or the
second argument of `.then()`. Delete this patch when upstream accepts rejection callbacks.

